  WHEN 3 THEN '1. Preheat oven to 200°C | 2. Cut sweet potatoes into cubes and roast 20 minutes | 3. Season salmon with lemon, garlic and olive oil | 4. Grill salmon 12 minutes | 5. Sauté asparagus 5 minutes | 6. Serve together with lemon wedge'
  WHEN 4 THEN '1. Mix oats, protein and chia seeds | 2. Add milk and mix well | 3. Add honey | 4. Let rest in fridge overnight | 5. Top with blueberries when serving'
  WHEN 5 THEN '1. Marinate chicken in yogurt and spices 30 minutes | 2. Sauté onion until golden | 3. Add chicken and sear 5 minutes | 4. Add tomatoes and simmer 20 minutes | 5. Cook rice separately | 6. Serve chicken over rice'
  WHEN 6 THEN '1. Mash bananas in bowl | 2. Beat eggs and add to bananas | 3. Add flour, protein and baking powder | 4. Heat non-stick pan | 5. Pour batter in small portions | 6. Cook 2 minutes each side'
  WHEN 7 THEN '1. Drain and flake tuna | 2. Cut tomatoes and cucumber into dice | 3. Rinse and drain chickpeas | 4. Mix all ingredients | 5. Crumble feta on top | 6. Drizzle with vinaigrette'
  WHEN 8 THEN '1. Blend dates and almonds until sticky | 2. Add oats and protein, blend briefly | 3. Add peanut butter | 4. Press into rectangular mold | 5. Sprinkle with chocolate chips | 6. Refrigerate 2 hours and cut into bars'
  WHEN 9 THEN '1. Cut turkey into strips | 2. Stir-fry turkey 5 minutes on high heat | 3. Add grated ginger and vegetables | 4. Stir-fry 5 more minutes | 5. Pour soy sauce | 6. Serve immediately'
  WHEN 10 THEN '1. Brown ground chicken 5 minutes | 2. Add diced vegetables | 3. Pour broth and bring to boil | 4. Add lentils and turmeric | 5. Simmer 25 minutes until tender | 6. Season and serve hot'
  WHEN 11 THEN '1. Grill chicken and cut into strips | 2. Mix yogurt and lemon for sauce | 3. Spread sauce on tortillas | 4. Add romaine, chicken and parmesan | 5. Roll wraps tightly | 6. Cut in half and serve'
  WHEN 12 THEN '1. Preheat oven to 180°C | 2. Beat eggs and milk together | 3. Finely chop all vegetables | 4. Mix vegetables and cheese with eggs | 5. Pour into muffin molds | 6. Bake 18-20 minutes'
  WHEN 13 THEN '1. Sauté onion and pepper 5 minutes | 2. Add beef and brown | 3. Add tomatoes and spices | 4. Simmer 30 minutes on low heat | 5. Add drained beans | 6. Simmer 10 more minutes'
  WHEN 14 THEN '1. Blend acai, banana, blueberries and milk | 2. Pour into bowl | 3. Top with granola in lines | 4. Add shredded coconut | 5. Decorate with fresh blueberries | 6. Serve immediately'
  WHEN 15 THEN '1. Cook rice according to instructions | 2. Sauté minced garlic 1 minute | 3. Add shrimp and cook 3 minutes | 4. Add zucchini rounds | 5. Stir-fry 4 more minutes | 6. Garnish with parsley and serve over rice'
  WHEN 16 THEN '1. Grate cauliflower and cook 5 minutes | 2. Drain and mix with egg and half the cheese | 3. Form crust and bake 20 minutes at 200°C | 4. Spread tomato sauce on base | 5. Add chicken and remaining cheese | 6. Bake 10 more minutes'
  WHEN 17 THEN '1. Cut beef into thin strips | 2. Blanch broccoli 3 minutes | 3. Sear beef 4 minutes on high heat | 4. Add broccoli and teriyaki sauce | 5. Cook noodles separately | 6. Serve garnished with sesame and green onion'
  WHEN 18 THEN '1. Cook quinoa and let cool | 2. Cut tomatoes and cucumber into small dice | 3. Finely chop mint | 4. Mix quinoa, vegetables and chickpeas | 5. Drizzle with lemon juice | 6. Refrigerate 1 hour before serving'
